Read and follow @AGENTS.md completely before planning, editing, reviewing, or
generating code. It is the canonical repository contract.

Authentication never implies authorization. For every feature, explicitly
define ownership, permissions, trust-boundary validation, recent MFA, audit and
outbox behavior, idempotency, and tests proving default denial.

Do not weaken AGENTS.md for convenience. Surface any conflict before changing
code.
